      "body": "## Motivation\n\nOn the Muse Spark Open branch, enabling LoRA with attention targets crashes the server at startup: the LoRA manager indexes modules by their `layers.N` position and sizes its tables from the language model's layer count, and the vision and audio towers' layers repeat the text projections' names (`q_proj`, `k_proj`, ...), so a tower layer index runs past the table (IndexError).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `MuseSparkForConditionalGeneration.should_apply_lora`: only the text decoder's `model.layers.N.` modules take LoRA.\n- `LoRAManager.init_lora_modules`: honor `should_apply_lora` when the base model defines it, as main already does for the VL models (the gate sits after the embed_tokens / lm_head handling for the same reason).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- Validated with the miles RL trainer (torchtitan backend) streaming rank-32 attention adapters into two engines serving `RadixArk/Muse-Spark-Open-last4-partial`: two rollouts, two adapter syncs, trainer-vs-engine log-prob abs diff 0.017 with routing replay.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41393523500](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41393523500)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41393523355](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41393523355)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41393523499](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41393523499)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
